Tool: Maven/Gradle

Use: Automates the building, packaging, and dependency management of applications.
Why Maven/Gradle?
Before Maven, Ant was widely used. Ant had no standardized project structure and required manually written scripts for dependencies.
Maven introduced convention over configuration and dependency management.
Gradle further improved by offering flexibility with Groovy scripting and better performance for large projects.
Drawbacks of Ant:
No built-in dependency management.
Tedious manual configurations.
